What the graphs were

{{ "%-17s %8s %7s %8s %11s  %6s %6s %7s %6s %6s %6s %6s  %9s %9s"|format("program", "deferred", "graphs", "largest", "largest node", "expr.", "tiled", "kernel", "fused", "given", "whole", "part", "lazy MB", "fused MB") }}
{{ "%-17s %8s %7s %8s %11s  %6s %6s %7s %6s %6s %6s %6s  %9s %9s"|format("", "ops", "", "graph", "elements", "", "", "calls", "nodes", "up", "writes", "writes", "written", "written") }}
{% for row in rows %}
{{ "%-17s %8d %7d %8d %12d  %6d %6d %7d %6d %6d %6d %6d  %9.1f %9.1f"|format(row.name, row.lazy.deferred, row.lazy.graphs, row.lazy.largest_graph, row.lazy.largest_node, row.stats.expressions, row.stats.tiled, row.stats.calls.values()|sum, row.stats.fused_nodes, row.stats.declined + row.stats.flagged, row.stats.whole_writes, row.stats.part_writes, row.lazy.written / bytes_per_mb, row.fused.written / bytes_per_mb) }}
{% endfor %}

`expr.`: expressions of two operations or more found in the graphs. `tiled`: those a kernel was planned for.
`fused nodes`: nodes computed inside a kernel call instead of by a call of their own. `given up`: kernel calls not
made, or dropped, because of the arrays' layout or a floating-point exception NumPy reports. `whole writes`,
`part writes`: writes computed by one NumPy call instead of a copy and a call. `MB written`: results the calls wrote.

